.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH "bead recurrence create" 1  "bead recurrence create " 
.SH NAME
bead recurrence create \- Create a new recurrence template
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBbead recurrence create\fR <\fB\-\-id\fR> <\fB\-\-title\fR> [\fB\-\-description\fR] <\fB\-\-base\-title\-template\fR> [\fB\-\-base\-description\fR] [\fB\-\-priority\fR] [\fB\-\-issue\-type\fR] [\fB\-\-labels\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Create an immutable recurrence template that defines how recurring issues should be created.
.PP
Templates define the structure for recurring issues including title templates, default priority,
issue type, and labels. Individual occurrences are created explicitly through the materialize
command, not automatically on schedules.
.PP
EXAMPLES:
  bead recurrence create \-\-id template\-001 \-\-title \*(AqDaily Review\*(Aq \-\-base\-title\-template \*(AqDaily Review {n}\*(Aq \-\-priority 2
  bead recurrence create \-\-id weekly\-planning \-\-title \*(AqWeekly Planning\*(Aq \-\-base\-title\-template \*(AqWeek {n} Planning\*(Aq \-\-labels \*(Aqweekly,planning\*(Aq
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-id\fR=\fIID\fR
Template ID
.TP
\fB\-\-title\fR=\fITITLE\fR
Template title
.TP
\fB\-\-description\fR=\fIDESCRIPTION\fR
Template description
.TP
\fB\-\-base\-title\-template\fR=\fIBASE_TITLE_TEMPLATE\fR
Title template for occurrences (use {n} for sequence number)
.TP
\fB\-\-base\-description\fR=\fIBASE_DESCRIPTION\fR
Description template for occurrences
.TP
\fB\-\-priority\fR=\fIPRIORITY\fR
Priority for created issues (0\-4, default 2)
.TP
\fB\-\-issue\-type\fR=\fIISSUE_TYPE\fR
Issue type for created issues (default \*(Aqtask\*(Aq)
.TP
\fB\-\-labels\fR=\fILABELS\fR
Comma\-separated list of labels to apply to occurrences
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
